[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 8"""
 date="2026-11-19T19:11:58Z"
 content="""
Reopening as there is still a bug. More proxy connections get opened than
closed, and the number can increase without bounds.

Can be reproduced with a proxyied external special remote,
using:

	while git-annex drop --force; git-annex get --from=origin-theremote -J2; done

The -J seems necessary, without concurrency there is no leak.

Looking at --debug, there are more "Opened proxy connection"
than "Closed proxy connection".

[[!commit cb5b92e9767fadec1baca0a4f463c52270b0ea3c]] had the problem,
so later changes (to use LRU for proxy connections) did not cause a new
bug.

Update: Fixed this one too.
"""]]
